# Curated from NASA/TM-20210011385 Appendix A (Tables A.1-A.6, report pp.103-113). One line per test.
# burn_flows: air-display velocities (cm/s) at which a flame was sustained, in order. L = low-flow plateau below anemometer floor (fan pot ~0.3-0.5).
# end: EXT=extinguished at end_flow | BLOW=blowoff at end_flow | NOIGN=no sustained flame at end_flow | END=still burning when test ended (burnout/stopped for other reason)
# end_flow: cm/s; L = below anemometer floor; 0 = fan turned off. Values with ~ are estimated from fan pot/fan display (see README).
